## Tech stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Language | C++23 (C++20 floor), no compiler extensions |
| Compiler | Clang (+ clang-tidy, clang-format, clangd); GCC as a cross-check only |
| Build | CMake 4.4.5 + Ninja, driven by CMakePresets |
| Dependencies | Conan 2.32.0 (Conan Center; everything pinned) |
| Test | GoogleTest + GoogleMock 1.18.0, discovered by CTest |
| Sanitizers | ASan + UBSan lane, separate TSan lane |
| Logging | spdlog (console + rotating file) |
| Scripting | Lua (embedded via sol2) when needed; Python for external tests only |
| Platform | Fedora, local tools only, no containers |

## Platform rules

- **No containers.** No Containerfile, no Dockerfile. Build, test, and run on the
  local machine with the CMake/Conan/CTest CLI.
- **Editors: CLion or VS Code** (clangd + CMake Tools). Every action is a CLI
  command; there is no IDE-only step.
- **Case-sensitive filesystem, `/` paths, LF line endings** (pinned in
  `.clang-format`).

## How to build

```bash
conan install . --output-folder=build --build=missing -s build_type=Debug
cmake --preset default
cmake --build --preset default
```

## How to test

```bash
ctest --preset default --output-on-failure          # all tests
ctest --preset default -R {{FILTER}}                 # by name regex

# checked lanes
cmake --preset asan-ubsan && cmake --build --preset asan-ubsan
ctest --preset asan-ubsan --output-on-failure        # ASan + UBSan

cmake --preset tsan && cmake --build --preset tsan
ctest --preset tsan --output-on-failure              # ThreadSanitizer (run alone)
```

## How to check style and analysis

```bash
clang-format --dry-run --Werror $(git ls-files '*.cpp' '*.hpp')   # style gate
run-clang-tidy -p build                                           # static analysis
./scripts/check-prereqs.sh                                         # toolchain gate
```

## Key file locations

```
CMakeLists.txt            ← top-level build: C++23, warnings-as-errors, targets
CMakePresets.json         ← default / asan-ubsan / tsan / release presets
conanfile.py              ← pinned dependencies + CMake generators
.clang-format             ← house style, LF line endings
.clang-tidy               ← enabled checks, warnings-as-errors
src/                      ← application + library code
tests/                    ← GoogleTest + GoogleMock test targets
scripts/check-prereqs.sh  ← toolchain gate (exits non-zero if missing)
build/                    ← CMake build tree + Conan generated files (gitignored)
logs/                     ← rotating log files (gitignored)
```

## Logging

The app logs through spdlog to the console and to a rotating file under `logs/`.
Read it after a failure with `grep -nE '\[error\]|\[warning\]' logs/{{PROJECT_NAME}}.log`.

## Conventions

- **Build/run success is a checkpoint, never the finish line.** Verify the observable
  effect (counts, output, metrics), not just the exit code.
- Warnings are errors; clang-tidy findings fail the build.
- Pin every Conan dependency to an exact version; survey with
  `conan search <name> -r conancenter` before bumping. No version ranges.
- GoogleTest + GoogleMock for tests. Boost.Test is not used. Catch2/doctest may be
  named as alternatives only.
- Idiomatic modern C++: RAII and smart pointers, `std::span`/`std::string_view`,
  ranges and `std::expected` where they clarify. Run `lgtm-idiomatic-review` before
  release.
- Lua (via sol2) for embedded scripting; Python only as an external test driver.
